PRIVACY POLICY FOR QUIT SMOKY
Last Updated: March 9, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how Quit Smoky ("we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, and discloses information about you when you use our mobile application on iOS.

1. Information We Collect
To provide the core features of the App (tracking your smoking cessation progress, health recovery milestones, and financial savings), we collect very limited data. Unlike many other apps, we do not require user accounts, nor do we request access to your location, camera, or microphone.

a. User Progress Data: Purpose: The App requires certain inputs (such as your quit date, daily cigarette consumption, and cigarette costs) to calculate your progress, achievements, and health milestones.
Processing: All of this personal tracking data is stored locally on your device. We do not transmit, store, or process this data on any external servers.

b. Usage Data & Diagnostics:
Purpose: To improve App stability and performance, we may collect anonymous crash reports and performance data.
Processing: This data is aggregated and not linked to your personal identity.

2. Third-Party Advertising & Tracking
To offer this App for free, we display advertisements provided by third-party networks, specifically Google AdMob.

a. Identifiers (IDFA): With your permission, we may access your device’s Advertising Identifier (IDFA) to deliver personalized ads that are more relevant to your interests.

b. App Tracking Transparency (ATT): In accordance with Apple's iOS requirements, we will request your permission to track your activity across other companies' apps and websites for advertising purposes.
Your Choice: You will see a prompt asking for this permission. You can tap "Ask App Not to Track" to decline.
Effect of Declining: If you decline, you will still see advertisements, but they may be less relevant to your interests. The App’s core tracking features and achievement systems will remain fully functional.

3. Data Sharing and Disclosure
We do not sell your personal data to third parties. We may share anonymous, aggregated usage data with third-party service providers (like Google AdMob) solely for the purpose of displaying advertisements and analyzing App performance.

For more details on how Google AdMob handles data, please review their policy: Google Privacy Policy

4. Age Restrictions and Children's Privacy
Target Audience: This App is designed to assist adults in quitting smoking and tracking their health progress. Due to references to tobacco use, the App is restricted to users who are 17 years of age or older. We do not knowingly collect, solicit, or maintain personal data from anyone under the age of 17. If we learn that we have collected personal data from a minor, we will take immediate steps to delete that information.

5. Security
We take reasonable measures to help protect information about you from loss, theft, misuse, and unauthorized access. Since the App functions by storing your quit progress locally on your device, your personal health and financial data are not transmitted to our servers.

6. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. If we make changes, we will notify you by revising the date at the top of the policy.

